{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 43, :comments ["<b>And I will meet you there.</b> I will appoint a meeting with them in speech — like a king who designates a place of meeting to speak with his servants there." "<b>And it shall be sanctified.</b> The Mishkan." "<b>Through My glory.</b> — that My Presence shall rest upon it. And its midrash aggadah: do not read בִּכְבֹדִי but בִּכְבוּדַי — 'through My honored ones' — here He hinted to him the death of the sons of Aharon on the day of its inauguration. And this is what is said: ״זֶה הוּא אֲשֶׁר דִּבֶּר יְהֹוָה לֵאמֹר בִּקְרֹבַי אֶקָּדֵשׁ״ — and where did He speak it? 'And it shall be sanctified through My glory' (Zevachim 115)."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:55:41.984692246Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}